      "id": 1,
      "text": "Vernonburg takes its name from James Vernon, who brought Salzburger emigrants to Georgia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernonburg%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Vernonburg sits about ten miles south of downtown Savannah, tucked at a sharp bend on the Vernon River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernonburg%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Georgia General Assembly incorporated Vernonburg in 1866, giving it official town status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernonburg%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town stretches along a narrow strip of riverfront property on the tidal Vernon River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernonburg%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Vernonburg is part of the Savannah metropolitan statistical area, linking it to the larger region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
